provider_responses.text:
Another important aspect is the user experience around transparency and reassurance.

When a software product handles a data-export request in the background, users may worry that something went wrong if they receive no immediate confirmation. A clear in-product message should confirm that the request was received, explain that preparation can take time, and provide an estimated delivery range. For example: “Your export is being prepared. We will email a download link to your account address when it is ready.”

The product should also make it easy for users to verify:
- the email address where the export link will be sent;
- whether the export is pending, ready, expired, or failed;
- when the request was made;
- whether another export request is already in progress;
- what to do if the message does not arrive.

This reduces unnecessary support requests and helps users feel confident that their information is being handled correctly.

